WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Happy belated birthday.
You just had one.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I did.
-All right.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, yeah,
now I'm getting to the age

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I don't want
to talk about birthdays.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:12.545
-Gotcha. Do you feel like you're
getting jaded as you get older?

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.647
-I am. Yeah, I am getting
a little bit more jaded.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:19.219
You know, I don't take things
as serious as I should, I guess.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But I've become more jaded,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.089
as far as Hollywood
and working and stuff like that.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's good.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
That happens
as you become older.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, more refined.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:32.032
Like, I was doing this TV show.
It's called "No Activity."

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.101 size:88% position:44%
It's on CBS streaming,
which it's a great show.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.771 size:84% position:42%
Please, try to watch it
if you get a chance.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.775
Because I have, you know,
child-support payments.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stuff like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when we were
shooting the show,

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
we did a scene where
we were downtown in L.A.,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:51.184
and the scene was supposed to be
me on my back on the ground.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had just
fallen off of a building.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so after
I got out of my trailer

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they took me to the set,
and they said,

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're gonna be
laying on the ground here,"

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.527 line:92%
I went, "Oh, okay, great.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this dirt --
Did we put this dirt here?

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.597 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Is this Hollywood dirt?"

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Show biz?

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:09.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the crew guy, he was just
like, "Hollywood dirt?"

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"What is that?"

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "You know, like,
dirt that we have,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.274 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that's like clean dirt."

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.442 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.744
He was like,
"No, this is downtown L.A. dirt.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.547
There's probably rat, you know,
droppings in the dirt

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:23.183
you're getting ready to lay in,
so good luck."

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.087 line:92%
-Your boys are, what, 16 and 18?

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-And athletes, play basket--

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
You coached a basketball team
this year?

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Well, not this year.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, a couple years ago.
-Gotcha.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And did you enjoy that?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
You know, it was weird,

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.900
because I don't know if you ever
coached your kids or whatever...

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're too young.
They're uncoachable.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, my kids was actually --
they were coachable.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.543
But it was weird, because
I'd never done it before.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.644 line:92%
So, like, the very first game --

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I did
a practice with them,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.747
sort of taught them
some basketball plays and stuff.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, the very first game,
they were playing,

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were down by
like 2 points.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was on the sideline,
and I was going, like,

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:05.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Man, their coach should call
time-out or something."

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Oh, wait, that's me.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:10.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm the coach.
Time-out, time-out!"

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:11.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it turned out
to be very fun and --

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.936
You know, like, if you're the
parent of one of the players,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.171 line:92%
you don't want to favor them.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.305 line:92%
You want to treat them equally.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:22.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my son Julian
was a very good player,

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we played
the championship --

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.044 line:92%
We got to the championship.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this was at the
Boys and Girls Club, not NBA.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't get me wrong.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.352
But there was --
We got to the championship game.

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:35.622
The team showed up to the game,
and they were all sweaty.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"What were you guys doing?"

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.692
And they said,
"Oh, we were playing basketball

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the alley."
And I'm like,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.563
"No, you're supposed to be
playing basketball now."

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.432 line:92%
"You have a championship game."

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.300 line:92%
Like, the Golden State Warriors,

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
they don't go and play
the Pistons for an hour..."

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
"...then they go play game 7."
-Right.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.474 line:92%
-And so we got into the game,

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.209 size:84% position:42%
and they started losing
'cause they were tired.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.411
The other kids were hot, and,
you know, they were winning.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:02.248
And then, I had to put the kids
who weren't that good in,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, you know,
that's just how it is.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some kids aren't that good.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.252 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.087
-And so I had to put those guys
in to sort of cover

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
until the good kids
could get some rest.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:14.494
And then, I kept my son in,
and then my son got hot.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:17.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Julian, he stole the ball,

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
took it down court,
laid it up like Gervin --

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:22.268
You know, like George Gervin,
like, finger-rolled it in.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Okay."
I'm not going to point out

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.306 size:81% position:41%
that he's doing better
than everybody else.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:29.576
I'm like, "Good job, young man,
keep going," you know.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:33.646
Next time, somebody else steals
the ball, passes it to him.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.750
He can go in for another layup,
but he stops back,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.853
does like a Steph Curry,
goes beyond the 3-point --

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
boom, 3 points.
Put us up.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.526
I didn't want to be too proud,
but when he came down the court,

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:49.162 size:84% position:42%
this time I was like,
"Yeah, down here, baby.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Down here."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah.
That's my boy!

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is my boy!"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could not keep it in.
-That's great.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nor should you.
-I know.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
when it was all over, we won.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
They gave us
these little medals and stuff,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is like the only award
I've ever won.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:05.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, a Boys and Girls Club
basketball necklace.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we got in the car
with my son and he was very --

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:14.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
he was happy and stuff.

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just tapped him
on the shoulder and I go,

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:19.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know what?
You won this that game for us.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You did that.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did that on your own,
and I'm really proud of you."

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I could not do that
without sobbing.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would've sobbed.
If the day comes that I ever

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.204
get to say something that nice,
I would just break down.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Dude, I was
so proud of those guys,

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.841 line:92%
'cause they played so hard.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:38.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I literally --
I was, like, up all night.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.647 line:92%
I was so full of adrenaline.

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm, like, calling people,
"Hey, guess who won

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Boys and Girls Club
basketball...?"

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.154
-Like, "Hold on. I'm gonna text
you a picture of my medal."

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.489 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.091
-And then, I put the medal
around my rearview mirror

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my car, you know.
-That's great.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it would just hit
the windshield

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it was so heavy.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "I don't care.
I'm so happy."

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is great.
"Schooled" is wonderful.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a spin-off
of "The Goldbergs."

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You play a principal.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Do you enjoy that?

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it a role you enjoy?
-I enjoy all roles.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, yes,
I enjoy this one quite a bit.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:15.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's fun to do.
I'm -- You know, I wasn't --

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know --
I've done a lot of --

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, people know me from
doing "Mean Girls"

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.754 size:81% position:41%
and stuff like that,
but this guy is, like,

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.157 size:84% position:42%
a little bit different.
He's a little edgier.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't know where I'm going

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:26.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
with this story.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I want to ask.
We're talking about edgier.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
Another role you're known for
is, of course,

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "SNL," the Ladies Man.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.801 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:35.601 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you've been thinking
about trying to reboot

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:40.973
the Ladies Man just to see
what life is like for him

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:43.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the post-#MeToo era.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think
it would be tough for him.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.513
-Yeah.
-'Cause I think he would always

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:50.450
have to retract every statement
that he made, you know?

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:54.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So he'd be like --
if he meet a woman in a bar

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something, he'd be like,
"Yeah, listen, baby.

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:59.826
I would love to, like, take you
out sometime if that's cool.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:02.729
But, listen, if you have a man
or something, I don't want to,

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, step on anybody toes
or anything.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:07.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, I would really love
to get you back to my place

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.634 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and make love to you.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, like, in a very nice
predictable way.

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:14.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course, you would
have say in our love-making.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:18.811
You would give me approval, and
then I would make the next step,

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.546 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
so, anyway...

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd like to buy you a drink,
if that's okay."

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.116 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think we all
would like to see that.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:26.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always so great
to have you here.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you, buddy.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Give it up for Tim Meadows,
everybody.

